[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"WorkManager & Background Execution Constraints in Android (Java)"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Background processing in Android has evolved significantly to preserve battery life and system performance. WorkManager is the recommended library for persistent, deferrable background work. Combined with Execution Constraints (Constraints class), it ensures tasks only run when optimal conditions are met."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Understanding WorkManager Constraints"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Constraints allow you to define the exact conditions under which your background work should execute. If constraints are not met, WorkManager pauses the task and automatically retries it once the environment satisfies the requirements."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Network Type: Requires specific connectivity (e.g., Unmetered, Connected, Not Roaming)."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Battery: Requires the device to have sufficient battery or be charging."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Storage: Pauses tasks when the device has low storage space."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Idle State: Requires the device to be idle (typically unused and screen off)."},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Creating a Worker Class"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"First, create a background task by extending the Worker class and overriding the doWork() method."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"public class UploadWorker extends Worker {
    public UploadWorker(@NonNull Context context, @NonNull WorkerParameters params) {
        super(context, params);
    }

    @NonNull
    @Override
    public Result doWork() {
        // Perform your background task here
        boolean success = uploadDataToServer();

        if (success) {
            return Result.success();
        } else {
            return Result.retry();
        }
    }

    private boolean uploadDataToServer() {
        // Implementation details
        return true;
    }
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Defining Constraints and Enqueuing Work"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Next, build your Constraints object using Constraints.Builder and pass it to your WorkRequest. In this example, the upload will only occur when the device is charging and connected to an unmetered Wi-Fi network."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"Constraints constraints = new Constraints.Builder()
    .setRequiredNetworkType(NetworkType.UNMETERED)
    .setRequiresCharging(true)
    .setRequiresBatteryNotLow(true)
    .build();

WorkRequest uploadWorkRequest = new OneTimeWorkRequest.Builder(UploadWorker.class)
    .setConstraints(constraints)
    .build();

WorkManager.getInstance(context).enqueue(uploadWorkRequest);"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Best Practices for Background Constraints"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Avoid overly strict constraints that may cause your work to be delayed indefinitely."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always handle Result.retry() gracefully with backoff criteria if network operations fail."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use PeriodicWorkRequest for repeating tasks, keeping constraints in mind to prevent battery drain."}]
